Write a Text File using Python

Aim

To open a text file and write contents using Python.

Requirements

- Raspberry Pi 4B
- Python 3

Description

The open() function opens test.txt in write mode.

- "open("test.txt", "w")" opens the file in write mode.
- "for i in range(1, 7)" generates six lines.
- "f.write(data)" writes the contents into the file.
- "f.close()" closes the file.

Execution

Run the program using:

"python3 write_txtfile.py"

To view the contents:

"cat test.txt"

Output

Line 1
Line 2
Line 3
Line 4
Line 5
Line 6

Conclusion

A text file is successfully written with six lines using Python.
